#!/bin/bash
set -eo pipefail

# Runs once, during `kamal setup`, right after docker has been installed on
# the server. There is nothing to install on top of it -- postgres arrives as
# an accessory and kamal creates its data directory itself -- so this prints
# the steps that setup does not do for you, in the order they have to happen.
cat <<'NOTE'

carscraper, first time on this server. What setup does not do:

  1. An A record for carscraper.diamondbay.nl pointing at the droplet.
     Without it kamal-proxy cannot get a certificate. pre-connect refuses to
     deploy until it resolves, so you will not get far without noticing.

  2. The database starts empty, so nothing is in the graph:

       bin/kamal accessory boot postgres
       ssh -fN -L 5433:127.0.0.1:5433 deployer@146.185.130.81
       pg_dump carscrape | psql -h localhost -p 5433 -U carscraper carscraper_production

     README.md has the same thing written out, including the postcodes.

  3. Scraping keeps happening here, not there, over that same tunnel -- the
     sites are friendlier to a home address than to a data centre.

NOTE
